{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449797-the-absent-spirit-conversion","id":1449797,"title":"The Absent spirit conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-27T07:50:26-07:00","id":1449797,"title":"The Absent spirit conversion","content":"If any of y'all have read Geist second edition you may have seen the appendix introducing the Absent..aka playable ghosts. I have read the rules for them and they seem mostly functional, so what I started pondering is if we could make something similar for Spirits. Playable spirits in other words using the basics of the Absent's rules. Any of you have thoughts about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T07:57:02-07:00","id":1449798,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure The Pack has additional content for making the Pack Totem playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T08:02:39-07:00","id":1449799,"title":"","content":"I mean it has content for advancing the Pack Totem but I am not sure if that counts as pc creation rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T08:22:12-07:00","id":1449802,"title":"","content":"While people have mentioned it, they tend to overlook a few things that make a spirit vastly different from a ghost and unplayable without making drastic enough changes that you're not playing a spirit.<br /> <br /> A ghost, for instance, is effectively the memories of a dead mortal. They remember mortal things, and had mortal experiences. Some of them are even unaware they are dead, believing themselves to just be living people doing their thing, unaware they've been doing the same thing every day for years.<br /> <br /> A spirit is immortal, and its interests and memories revolve almost entirely around its Resonance. They have never been human, and even those who have Claimed humans do not know what it's like to live a normal life. Their perspectives are so different they're often described as alien, or mad. They also don't have the same background as each other. A computer spirit borne from the computer I'm using right now would have had a drastically different background from the tree spirit outside my window, and both would have an incredibly different experience borne from a dream spirit that was borne and went into dormancy in the few hours of my sleep. Contrast this with ghosts, who providing they're of humans, have at least experienced more human-understandable concepts, like mortality and sickness, the tastes of different types of food or drink, family, a culture and civilization, love and lust, all things that spirits don't get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T08:31:54-07:00","id":1449805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449797-the-absent-spirit-conversion?p=1449802#post1449802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While people have mentioned it, they tend to overlook a few things that make a spirit vastly different from a ghost and unplayable without making drastic enough changes that you're not playing a spirit.<br /> <br /> A ghost, for instance, is effectively the memories of a dead mortal. They remember mortal things, and had mortal experiences. Some of them are even unaware they are dead, believing themselves to just be living people doing their thing, unaware they've been doing the same thing every day for years.<br /> <br /> A spirit is immortal, and its interests and memories revolve almost entirely around its Resonance. They have never been human, and even those who have Claimed humans do not know what it's like to live a normal life. Their perspectives are so different they're often described as alien, or mad. They also don't have the same background as each other. A computer spirit borne from the computer I'm using right now would have had a drastically different background from the tree spirit outside my window, and both would have an incredibly different experience borne from a dream spirit that was borne and went into dormancy in the few hours of my sleep. Contrast this with ghosts, who providing they're of humans, have at least experienced more human-understandable concepts, like mortality and sickness, the tastes of different types of food or drink, family, a culture and civilization, love and lust, all things that spirits don't get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran on the assumption that people asking this question are quite willing to hopscotch this consideration.<br /> <br /> If I were to be cynical, I assume the perceived benefit for many is getting play a character who &quot;has permission&quot; to completely ignore the humanism themes of the games, but I'm not <i>quite</i> willing to assume that's always the appeal. Heaven knows I played a familiar once because I wanted to approach that notion from a different angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T09:16:52-07:00","id":1449811,"title":"","content":"So I agree that normal spirits are not good for pc concepts as is, so I have put the mind cauldron to work and the logical solution is to find a way to make spirits get a more human outlook. So I have a growing concept in mind where there is a type of spirit that get's &quot;broken&quot; by being forcibly given an integrity score and a touchdown or something along those lines. Something to make them say something about the human condition but from the outside looking in. Like how the Absent are different from your average ghost these Broken Spirits would be the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T10:02:28-07:00","id":1449814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449797-the-absent-spirit-conversion?p=1449811#post1449811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I agree that normal spirits are not good for pc concepts as is, so I have put the mind cauldron to work and the logical solution is to find a way to make spirits get a more human outlook. So I have a growing concept in mind where there is a type of spirit that get's &quot;broken&quot; by being forcibly given an integrity score and a touchdown or something along those lines. Something to make them say something about the human condition but from the outside looking in. Like how the Absent are different from your average ghost these Broken Spirits would be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>An integrity score or integrity-alike might be overneeded.<br /> <br /> Giving advice based on that aforementioned time I played a familiar (in Mage the Ascension, a time-spirit riding shotgun in a raven, for context), the two big things I relied on was being a spirit with experience with humanity (Wednesday was an old spirit* who had been a familiar to at least one other mage before the PC they were bonded to, and thus was expected to have a certain amount of aping going on, albeit with a catch[particularly, tenses never made sense and they would switch them around all the time]) and picking concepts that lend well to the illusion of humanity(okay, time may not intuitive, but we leaned into as a lens for interactions, and some concepts are great for it).<br /> <br /> The big thing is getting the player's buy-in-if the player understand the goals and is willing to play to it, that non-humanity is a easier to tackle.<br /> <br /> *who turned out to be a timeless demon, but that was the Storyteller's call that I gave to him, not a personal decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:50:10-07:00","id":1449848,"title":"","content":"I kind of read some of the spirits in the Mage: the Awakening supplement Boston Unveiled as kind of being like they want to act like humans to the best that they understand them, so I think that could be an angle to go for in certain conceptual spirits. Not quite getting it, but feeling it's a necessity to be what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T19:51:51-07:00","id":1451004,"title":"","content":"This is a fun idea. The way I'd do it is, sometimes the resonance from a particular human is harvested enough by a single spirit that it becomes a kind of imitation magath of that person, and assumes some elements of their identity. But once it's been infected by humanity it can't easily switch back to being a pure spirit in its motivations, and starts developing more human behavior patterns and agendas over time. Just like the Absent, it starts needing (or at least benefiting from) particular memories rather than generic resonance.<br /> <br /> Say the temptation on the spirit's end is, if it learns how to harvest memories, it gets the full diversity of that memory and all its emotional resonance, whereas normally it is limited only to certain flavors. To the point that these rare spirits might eventually completely &quot;cross over&quot; to human. I'd borrow the &quot;Drop-Ins&quot; concept from Stephen King, perhaps. But no drop-in ever completely shakes the spirit side or completely understands the human side. Give 'em a morality stat called Mimicry.<br /> <br /> To keep it sinister and horrible, Mimics have to displace a human, hollowing them out entirely and stepping into the now-empty shell, and then the now-spiritualized human soul takes the spirit's place in the Shadow. Hell, maybe Mimics are just a sub-class of spirits that absorb too much diverse resonance linked to a certain theme, and <i>anything </i>can be turned into a Mimic. Unlike a normal possessed whatever, this is a one-way trip; the spirit gets extended or permanent manifestation as a new object or person or animal or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 06-04-2021, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}